From c959ff03df8aba0bbf2fccf2dc962687611e0751 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: manerger <filidog82@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 22:56:04 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 23/23] mb/asustek_computer/k53sc: Enable the PCH thermal
 controller

autoport recorded "device ref thermal off", but the hardware does have the
controller at D31:F6. Enable it so the device tree matches the board.

This is a correctness fix rather than a functional one, and worth saying so:
Linux will not bind a driver to it. intel_pch_thermal's PCI aliases begin at
8086:8C24 (Lynx Point); there is none for Cougar Point's 8086:1C24, so the
module loads and claims nothing. No new thermal zone appears.

Verified on hardware: 00:1f.6 now enumerates as "6 Series/C200 Series Chipset
Family Thermal Management Controller [8086:1c24]" with the board subsystem ID,
and no driver bound. CPU temperature continues to come from x86_pkg_temp and
the EC, as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/mainboard/asustek_computer/k53sc/devicetree.cb | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/mainboard/asustek_computer/k53sc/devicetree.cb b/src/mainboard/asustek_computer/k53sc/devicetree.cb
index ec1f92de66..2d55e15fc8 100644
--- a/src/mainboard/asustek_computer/k53sc/devicetree.cb
+++ b/src/mainboard/asustek_computer/k53sc/devicetree.cb
@@ -110,7 +110,8 @@ chip northbridge/intel/sandybridge # FIXME: GPU registers may not always apply.
 			end
 			device ref sata2 off
 			end
-			device ref thermal off
+			device ref thermal on
+				subsystemid 0x1043 0x1277
 			end
 		end
 	end
